{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/437745-noctuku-update-for-second-edition","id":437745,"title":"Noctuku Update for Second Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-11T17:29:56-07:00","id":437745,"title":"Noctuku Update for Second Edition","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>EDIT:</b> This is still incomplete, but I decided to update what I had so people can give feedback. I plan to make two more dots in Phagia.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Noctuku hav</span><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">e always been one of my favorite Bloodlines, so I decided to try and update it. I hope to comeback to this and add Devotions that bring back some of the powers that Phagia granted, but right now I don't think I'm up to that challenge. I'm sure I've made some serious mistakes, so please point them out so I can fix them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Noctuku</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Noctuku are considered monsters among monsters by other Kindred because their preferred prey is other vampires. Because of this, Noctuku usually live a solitary existence to protect themselves from other vampires and other vampires from them. Noctuku who abhor a solitary existence usually group together into tight-knit clutches. These clutches are surprisingly stable do to the precautions and ritualistic behavior taken on to reduce the chances of a self-destructive feeding frenzy.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Clan:</b> Nosferatu</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Nickname:</b> Bogeymen, Cannibals</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Disciplines:</b> Nightmare, Obfuscate, Resilience, Vigor</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Bloodline Bane:</b> Those who join the Noctuku bloodline soon find that their hunger has twisted and grown. All Noctuku suffer from Vitae Addiction and can never rid themselves of it. In addition, Noctuku find that they hunger for the flesh of their prey. If a Noctuku fails to deal at least 1 lethal damage by eating the flesh of his victims for a week, he gains the Bestial Condition. A Noctuku who has gained the Bestial Condition and has not eaten for a week must drink the blood of a victim and eat at least 3 lethal damage worth of their flesh before he can resolve it. Even if he has had the Bestial Condition within the last month, he can still gain it from not eating the flesh of his prey. Despite their need to eat flesh, they cannot actually digest it and will throw it up like anything else they eat.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Bloodline Gift: Apex Predator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">As a predator of predators, the Noctuku often can't help viewing Kindred like other vampires view mortals. The Beast of a Noctuku is an all-devouring thing that is difficult to deny, but it does provide the tools needed to hunt its favored prey. All Noctuku have the Vitaevore Advantage and may purchase the Phagia Merit to increase their ability to feed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Vitaevore</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Do to the particularity of their diet, Noctuku are better at tracking other vampires and are somewhat more resistant to the Vinculum. All Noctuku gain the benefits of the Weakened Bond Merit and can track other Kindred by tasting their blood as if they were mortal.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Merit: Phagia (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022; Style)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Prerequisite:</b> Noctuku</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Your Noctuku character has begun to heed the secrets his Beast whispers to him. Known to the Noctuku as Phagia, these techniques assist in hunting the forbidden prey: Kindred. Phagia transforms the Vinculum from a means of control into a tool for feeding. While a Noctuku still feels all the love and slavish devotion anyone under the Vinculum does, he also feels a terrible hunger for the one who has him bound.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Devouring Maw (\u2022): </b>Whenever your character succeeds on a Feed move, he may deal an extra point of lethal damage to his victims as he tears and swallows their flesh along with their blood. Anybody who has had damage dealt to them by Devouring Maw while being fed upon gains the Scarred Condition as if they were mortal.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Just a Taste (\u2022\u2022): </b>If<b> y</b>our character is under the Vinculum, he develops blood sympathy towards anyone who has bonded him. A stage-one blood bond is treated as three times removed, stage-two as two times removes, and stage-three as one removed. If your character already has a higher level of blood sympathy to someone than this Merit would grant, use the higher one instead.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Dark Hunger (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> Your character gains a bonus to tracking and detect blood sympathy rolls against whoever has him under the Vinculum equal to what stage he's at. He also gains a bonus to his Humanity roll for harming someone who has bound him equal to the stage of the Vinculum he's under as long as he's frenzying.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Drawback: </b>Your character also gains a penalty to resisting frenzy when hungry or starving equal to the stage of the Vinculum he is at as long as he is near someone who has bonded him. Use the largest penalty available if your character is near multiple people who have bonded him. If your character frenzies do to hunger he will try to feed from the person who he has the highest bond with first if possible.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","user":"Xenorath","date":". 03-12-2015, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T19:59:44-07:00","id":437921,"title":"","content":"I don't think Scarred is appropriate for Kindred, and they don't take Swooning (the kiss applies to mortals and the living). Also, the first dot seems only to apply to Kindred as its effects always occur against humans. The anti-vinculum nature of it runs counter to the concept of the vinculum, your character would basically not use it due to the vinculum. Heavy social penalties and the emotional influence involved with the vinculum. You would also wreck your humanity in short order targeting someone who has a vinculum against you. If anything, I would say increase bonus' against a vinculum taking hold, rather than targeting someone who has you under a vinculum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T20:53:17-07:00","id":437969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/437745-noctuku-update-for-second-edition?p=437921#post437921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Scarred is appropriate for Kindred, and they don't take Swooning (the kiss applies to mortals and the living).</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the section on feeding, you can give a vampire the Swooning or Scarred Conditions if you spend a point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/437745-noctuku-update-for-second-edition?p=437921#post437921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the first dot seems only to apply to Kindred as its effects always occur against humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should probably reword it. You can use it against a mortal, your just dealing an extra point of lethal damage to them for the convenience of not having to eat them after you get done drinking their blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/437745-noctuku-update-for-second-edition?p=437921#post437921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The anti-vinculum nature of it runs counter to the concept of the vinculum, your character would basically not use it due to the vinculum. Heavy social penalties and the emotional influence involved with the vinculum. You would also wreck your humanity in short order targeting someone who has a vinculum against you. If anything, I would say increase bonus' against a vinculum taking hold, rather than targeting someone who has you under a vinculum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take that into consideration. The idea was while you love the person who bound you, it also makes your Beast want to eat him more. I'm thinking about moving the whole hunger frenzy thing from the 5th dot down to the 4th dot and having it increase your chances of entering hunger frenzy when your around the person who put you under the Vinculum.<br /> <br /> Oh, I just realized a problem, your right about the breaking point thing. Before I just considered it a part of the package, but who would want to purchase a merit that makes you better at killing your Humanity? How about I work something in that gives you a large bonus to making your Humanity roll if you hurt your regnant?<br /> <br /> What I was trying to go for was while you can blood bond a Noctuku, it probably isn't a good idea to do so long term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T21:03:40-07:00","id":437976,"title":"","content":"I would make their Gift that ghoul/mortal merit that treats them as a step lower/dulls the emotional component of it.<br /> <br /> I think it's a cool idea to base it around them getting the Vinculum. Getting in a bite to gain the Vinculum then using it to hunt them down or something like that seems as terrifying as the Noctuku ought to be, reinforcing a stalker-like aspect of the Bloodline. How it fucks with their Humanity is just icing on the horror cake.<br /> <br /> I'd maybe use Phagia to give stuff like the 3rd dot, except you track them through a blood sympathy that comes from their Vinculum to that person, maybe gain bonuses based on the level of Vinculum/the Breaking Points, stuff like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 03-12-2015, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T22:29:17-07:00","id":438052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/437745-noctuku-update-for-second-edition?p=437976#post437976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would make their Gift that ghoul/mortal merit that treats them as a step lower/dulls the emotional component of it.<br /> <br /> I think it's a cool idea to base it around them getting the Vinculum. Getting in a bite to gain the Vinculum then using it to hunt them down or something like that seems as terrifying as the Noctuku ought to be, reinforcing a stalker-like aspect of the Bloodline. How it fucks with their Humanity is just icing on the horror cake.<br /> <br /> I'd maybe use Phagia to give stuff like the 3rd dot, except you track them through a blood sympathy that comes from their Vinculum to that person, maybe gain bonuses based on the level of Vinculum/the Breaking Points, stuff like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's some great advice. How do these updated first three dots of Phagia look?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Devouring Maw (\u2022): </b>Whenever your character succeeds on a Feed move, he may deal a point of lethal damage to his victim. Anybody who has had damage dealt to them by Devouring Maw while being fed upon gains the Scarred Condition as if they were mortal.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Just a Taste (\u2022\u2022): </b>Ifyour character is under the Vinculum, he develops blood sympathy towards anyone who has bonded him. A stage-one blood bond is treated as three times removed, stage-two as two times removes, and stage-three as one removed. If your character already has a higher level of blood sympathy to someone than this Merit would grant, use the higher one instead.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Dark Hunger (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> Your character gains a bonus to tracking and detect blood sympathy rolls against whoever has him under the Vinculum equal to what stage he's at.<br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Your character also gains a penalty to resisting frenzy when hungry or starving equal to the stage of the Vinculum he is at as long as he is near someone who has bonded him. Use the largest penalty available if your character is near multiple people who have bonded him. If your character frenzies do to hunger he will try to feed from the person who he has the highest bond with first if possible.</span></span><br /> <br /> I know the wording on Dark Hunger is seriously jacked up regardless of whether it is mechanically sound or not, so any advice on that would be welcomed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T22:47:14-07:00","id":438075,"title":"","content":"I think those are neat. I applaud your use of the level of the blood bond as the dice bonus, makes it nice and distinct from many other mechanics they might use.<br /> <br /> Some feedback on Devouring Maw: You already do a Lethal damage (at least) if you successfully Feed on someone. If you successfully feed on someone, you're already inflicting Scarred, and if you want it on Kindred, you just have to spend a Willpower to do it. I feel like this dot could use a bit more <i>oomph </i>to it. I suggest focusing on the cannibal aspect of the Noctuku. Maybe when they Feed, they inflict an additional lethal damage (while gaining the extra 1 Vitae), and it represents them tearing the flesh from their enemy and consuming it? Perhaps if they get the Vinculum this way, it gives them a particular advantage, as opposed to less forceful means, like consensual feeding.<br /> <br /> I feel like you have the right idea, just uncertain about the mechanic to attach to it.<br /> <br /> I also feel their Bloodline Bane could be simplified. I think I need a bit to give an alternative suggestion, but I'd definitely give a direct weakness, then also discuss how their feeding habits frequently puts them in a traumatizing situation with regards to the vinculum and breaking it to harm somebody. Hell, the Drawback on Phagia might cover it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 03-12-2015, 01:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T00:00:50-07:00","id":438107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/437745-noctuku-update-for-second-edition?p=438075#post438075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMaybe when they Feed, they inflict an additional lethal damage (while gaining the extra 1 Vitae), and it represents them tearing the flesh from their enemy and consuming it?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually what I was trying to do. From what I could gather, vampires don't take damage when fed upon, they only lose Vitae which is why I specified the point of lethal. The main reason I included the Scarred Condition for free is because I wanted to emphasis that the Noctuku are vampires among vampires, but if you think it should go I'll consider getting rid of it.<br /> As it is right now it only kicks in if you eat their flesh while drinking their blood. I think gaining some sort of bonus from getting the Vinculum thhrough it is a good idea and I'll see if I can think of something.<br /> <br /> I also agree that the Drawback is a bit complicated, but I'm not 100% sure how I can fix it yet. I will also add something to the entire write up about how awful the Vinculum feeding cycle is.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I probably should have mentioned I changed the Advantage:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Vitaevore</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Do to the particularity of their diet, Noctuku are better at tracking other vampires and are somewhat more resistant to the Vinculum. All Noctuku gain the benefits of the Weakened Bond Merit and can track other Kindred by tasting their blood as if they were mortal.</span></span><br /> <br /> The idea is that while you eventually gain the power to find your prey through blood sympathy, tracking through scent is more reliable once they are nearby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","user":"Xenorath","date":". 03-12-2015, 03:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}